* TopMetal2 microstrip models at 122 GHz (RLGC, 20 lumped sections; R is the loss at 122 GHz, constant in frequency).
* Source: the public interface rows of the reference design (RF interconnect: 13 um line 50.9 ohm, 1.00 dB/mm, 6.58 ps/mm)
* and its line table (6 um 65.5 ohm 1.00 dB/mm eps_eff 3.87; 23 um 38.4 ohm 0.78 dB/mm eps_eff 3.89), simulated with openEMS
* over a two-layer slotted Metal1 + Metal2 ground. Use: X<name> a b tm2_w13 len=<metres>, len <= 1e-3. Ground is node 0.
* The series resistors are noisy (thermal noise of the line loss). Do not change this file.

* 6 um TopMetal2: 65.5 ohm, 1.00 dB/mm, eps_eff 3.87 (6.56 ps/mm)
.subckt tm2_w6 a b len=100e-6
.param ls={4.296800e-07*len/20} cs={1.001527e-10*len/20} rs={1.508174e+04*len/20}
